# Faultline APP-TIER per-deploy image tags — the compose env-file that rides
# in the S3 deploy bundle (NOT user-data), so an image bump never reprovisions the
# host.
#
# Three images, one compose stack: the QuantLib backend (one image serving every
# entrypoint — pricer API, marketdata, risk, scenariogen, sizing, governance), the
# QuantLib-free BFF, and the nginx SPA.
#
# scripts/deploy_qlp_bundle.py substitutes ${REGISTRY} (the in-account ECR host,
# derived from STS at upload time — which is why the real account id is not
# committed here) and uploads the result to s3://<qlp-data>/deploy/deploy.env.
# app-deploy.sh passes it as compose's SECOND --env-file, so these win over the
# image placeholders in docker-compose.aws.yml.
#
# TO BUMP AN IMAGE: edit a tag below (or pass --tag to the script to fill
# arm64-SETME), re-run scripts/deploy_qlp_bundle.py, then `systemctl restart
# app.service` on the host (SSM). No Terraform, no reprovision. Tags are immutable
# (never :latest); a tag is a reliable record of what runs.
QLP_BACKEND_IMAGE=${REGISTRY}/genai-dev/qlp-backend:arm64-SETME
QLP_BFF_IMAGE=${REGISTRY}/genai-dev/qlp-bff:arm64-SETME
QLP_UI_IMAGE=${REGISTRY}/genai-dev/qlp-ui:arm64-SETME
